{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"natural number natural number","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md","fileName":"Natural Number.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Natural Number","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 23:41\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Number Systems and Arithmetic]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Closure Property","Integer","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"natural number natural number","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md","fileName":"Natural Number.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Natural Number","heading":"Natural Number","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A natural number is a member of the ordered collection\n\n$$\\mathbb{N}=\\{0,1,2,3,\\ldots\\}.$$\n\nNatural numbers are used to count objects and identify positions in an order. Addition and multiplication of two natural numbers produce another natural number, so these operations satisfy the [[Closure Property]] on this set. Subtraction and division can leave it: (3-5) is not natural, and neither is (3/5). Extending natural numbers with opposites produces the [[Integer]]s.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Closure Property","Integer","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"natural number natural number","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Natural Number.md","fileName":"Natural Number.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Natural Number","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[algebraessentials.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Number Systems and Arithmetic","Closure Property","Integer","algebraessentials.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}